    <string name="performance_advice_title">Suggested next step · guidance only; no automatic changes</string>
    <string name="performance_advice_cpu">System-wide CPU pressure does not prove the game itself is CPU-bound. Try one CPU-heavy in-game setting or manually close an unused app; NitroBoost makes no change here.</string>
    <string name="performance_advice_gpu">Reported GPU and frame evidence suggests graphics pressure. If needed, lower render scale or effects inside the game; NitroBoost does not control the GPU or change this setting.</string>
    <string name="performance_advice_memory">Android reports system-wide memory pressure. Manually close apps you do not need; NitroBoost will not stop apps automatically.</string>
    <string name="performance_advice_thermal">Reduce boost intensity or pause and let the device cool. Thermal safeguards take priority; no thermal override is suggested.</string>
    <string name="performance_advice_network">TCP probes and system retransmissions do not measure the game-server route or packet-loss percentage. Check the game server/network before changing anything.</string>
    <string name="performance_advice_display">Match the game frame cap or configured target to the active display refresh rate; NitroBoost does not force a refresh rate.</string>
    <string name="performance_advice_mixed">Several domains are involved. Adjust one in-game setting at a time and re-check measurements; keep thermal protection in priority.</string>
    <string name="performance_advice_healthy">Measurements are within the configured target. Keep settings unchanged unless fresh evidence shows a different state.</string>
    <string name="performance_advice_unknown">Reliable, fresh data is not available yet. Wait for more samples or check sensor/usage access; no bottleneck is inferred.</string>
